{% from "shared/macros.md.j2" import entity_line %}
{% from "fate/_events.md.j2" import events_by_world %}
{% set distortions = [
  "confuses who did it",
  "reverses the order of an event",
  "makes a small event large or a large one small",
  "credits the deed to someone or something else"
] %}
{{ world_header }}

{% if world_events %}
WHAT REALLY HAPPENED DURING AGE {{ age }} (world by world; a people lived only what happened in its own world):
{{ events_by_world(world_events, rules.fate.voices_events_chars, rules.context.budget_trim_min_chars) | trim }}
{% else %}
WHAT REALLY HAPPENED DURING AGE {{ age }}:
{{ age_events[:rules.fate.voices_events_chars] if age_events else "(a quiet age)" }}
{% endif %}
{% if chains %}

CHAINS OF CAUSE (each people tells why from its own side):
{{ chains | join("\n") }}
{% endif %}

{% if tales %}
TALES UNDER WAY IN LIVES THIS AGE (the historian who tells these events tells them as parts of these tales, from its own people's side):
{% for tale in tales %}
- {{ tale.subject }}: a tale of {{ tale.template }}, now at its {{ tale.stage }}{% if tale.outcome != "open" %}, ended {{ tale.outcome }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if payoffs %}
PAYOFFS THIS AGE (each pays off what was set up in an earlier age; a people that tells it may tell it as that payoff):
{% for payoff in payoffs %}
- the {{ payoff.kind }} set up in age {{ payoff.since }}{% if payoff.subject %} about {{ payoff.subject }}{% endif %}: {{ payoff.text }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if historians %}
HISTORIANS (for each, this age's account from its own people's side; do not open with "We …", do not repeat the opening of the previous account; each account is written by the historian named for it, a mortal of that people{% if world_events %}; every historian tells as "we" ONLY the events of its own world, never another world's event as if it befell its own people, at most as news from afar{% endif %}):
{% for entry in historians %}
people_id {{ entry.people.id }}{% if entry.world %} (its world: {{ entry.world }}){% endif %}: {{ entity_line(entry.people) }}
Its account is told by: {{ entry.historian }}, {{ entry.historian_who }}, a mortal of this people.
{% if entry.society %}
{{ entry.society }}
{% endif %}
{% if entry.previous_opening %}
Previous historian: {{ entry.previous_historian if entry.previous_historian else "name unknown" }} (Age {{ entry.previous_age }}); the previous account opened like this: «{{ entry.previous_opening[:rules.fate.historian_opening_chars] }}…»
{% endif %}
{% if not loop.last %}

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if beliefs %}
BELIEFS (how each people tells of this god by the name it gave the god; each belief's distortion is written in the form given to it, no two beliefs use the same sentence construction):
{% for pair in beliefs %}
people_id {{ pair.people_id }} {{ pair.people_name }} → son_id {{ pair.son_id }}, in truth {{ pair.son_name }}, {{ pair.son_title }} ({{ pair.domain_1 }}/{{ pair.domain_2 }}); {% if pair.known_name %}this people calls the god "{{ pair.known_name }}"{% else %}this people has not yet given the god a name: give one with the sounds of the {{ pair.people_name }} people's language{% endif %}. Form of distortion: {{ distortions[(pair.people_id + pair.son_id + loop.index0) % (distortions | length)] }}.{% if pair.son_id == 0 %} This is the creator of all the gods; how they know the creator follows their own beliefs and what the creator has done among them.{% elif pair.worshipped %} They worship this god.{% else %} They do not worship this god; how they regard the god follows what the god has done among them.{% endif %}

{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
Historians should use their own peoples' names and lexicon. Beliefs should name the god by the name the people gave; they know only what this people saw or heard.
